                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system and trough near the western border will move eastwards today, clearing to the east later on Tuesday. A ridge towards the east of the state will weaken and move southeast as this system moves though. Another high will develop south of the state on Wednesday. Another trough extends into the far west of SA later Thursday.</text>
                <text type="preamble">Wind and wave forecasts are averages. Wind gusts can be 40 per cent stronger than the forecast, and stronger still in squalls and thunderstorms. Maximum waves can be twice the forecast height.</text>
